WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.680
Why did Wendy and Marty make that tough decision?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.720
What did the car crash really mean? What was up&nbsp;
with Wendy's time in the mental health hospital?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.120
Here's the ending of Ozark Season&nbsp;
4 explained. Spoilers ahead!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.920
While Sam Dermody might be gullible, we can all&nbsp;
agree that he still deserves a pleasant send-off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.240
Throughout the series, the main characters&nbsp;
move him wherever they need him, resulting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.320
in him working for Ruth at the Lazy-O Motel, a&nbsp;
property she uses to launder money for Darlene.
 &nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.440
"And now look at you. Look,&nbsp;
you've landed this great new job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.840
Worked out better than I'd hoped."
 
Sam ultimately escapes the Ozark madness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.760
by looking toward a higher power. He's baptized&nbsp;
and leaves town with Nathan and the congregation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.080
meaning that he will no longer unknowingly&nbsp;
aid and abet the main characters in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.600
crimes. At least one character appears to have&nbsp;
a happily-ever-after at the ending of "Ozark."
 &nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.360
In the final hour, Wendy makes a bold move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.240
by checking herself into a mental health facility&nbsp;
to get her kids back. Charlotte and Jonah had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.080
planned on going into Nathan's custody, giving him&nbsp;
a victory –- albeit short-lived –- over Wendy.
 &nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.920
"I know he's better than mom."
 
"Jonah."
 &nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.400
"What? He is, and besides, this will&nbsp;
be a good chance to get to know him."
 &nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.240
Credit where credit's due, Ruth does play a&nbsp;
major role in keeping the four Byrdes together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.200
when she threatens Nathan at gunpoint in his&nbsp;
motel room. But it's Wendy who makes an emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.680
gambit to get the kids back on her side.
When Jonah and Charlotte go visit her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.200
she redeems herself by coming&nbsp;
clean about her brother's death.
 &nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:44.400
"It's my fault. All of it."
 
At long last, she takes responsibility for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.800
his demise and apologizes to her kids, which is&nbsp;
likely all Jonah ever wanted to hear. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.800
Nathan leaves the Ozarks with the rest of&nbsp;
the congregation while Jonah and Charlotte&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.280
stay by their parents.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:02.320
Omar spends most of the final season behind&nbsp;
bars, and when he's finally released from jail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.520
he's driven to the middle of&nbsp;
nowhere and killed by an officer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.320
Marty, proving to be one step ahead&nbsp;
of everyone for the entire series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.040
eerily foreshadowed Omar's death when he told&nbsp;
Camila that if Omar were to be killed while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.600
transferring, it would be considered fate.
With Omar officially out of the picture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.400
the cartel is turned over to Camila. Omar&nbsp;
was supposed to be released from prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.000
transferred to Mexico, and then broken out to head&nbsp;
the cartel once again. But Camila is the one who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.040
gets the final deal with the FBI, resulting in&nbsp;
Omar becoming little more than a pawn in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.120
Byrdes' eventual bid for freedom.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.600
Season 4 kicks off with the Byrdes getting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.800
a major car crash. However, this scene&nbsp;
isn't revisited until the series finale.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.600
Although it's common for fans to try to make&nbsp;
every single detail and decision meaningful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.400
this accident feels more like a misdirect&nbsp;
rather than a major plot development.&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.560
The car accident, however, does indicate&nbsp;
how much the family has been through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.600
as it doesn't seem to phase them as much as fans&nbsp;
might expect. Though they're initially startled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.200
they then hop in a cab, head home, and seemingly&nbsp;
aren't affected one bit by the accident.&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.840
However, while it doesn't affect the plot much,&nbsp;
it does offer the opportunity for conflicting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.680
viewpoints. Navarro's priest looks at the accident&nbsp;
as a sign of the Byrde's lives being destructive.
 &nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.440
"How many times does God have to&nbsp;
point at you before you take notice?"
 &nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.880
Wendy, on the other hand, views the event as&nbsp;
proof that her family is going to be fine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.120
They are alive at the end, although Jonah&nbsp;
has to murder someone to make it happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.400
So…who knows what comes next for the Byrdes.&nbsp;
Ultimately, it may be up to the audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.840
to decide which meaning is true — sort of a&nbsp;
choose-your-own-adventure of thematic symbolism.
 &nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.680
Camila may have taken over the cartel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.480
but she still doesn't know who killed Javi.&nbsp;
For just a little while, it looks like things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.400
will stay that way, until a big mood change&nbsp;
happens at the gala: Camila pressures Clare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.600
to give up Javi's real killer.
 
"It was Ruth Langmore."
 &nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.520
Camila then threatens to take out the Byrdes'&nbsp;
children if they attempt to warn Ruth in any way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.720
And in the end, they choose their&nbsp;
own safety over Ruth's life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.920
Needless to say, the ending of "Ozark" is&nbsp;
bittersweet for the Byrdes and audiences.
 &nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.320
"What if this is too much to bear?"
 
 &nbsp;

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.200
"It won't be."

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.240
Entering the series finale, it appears that Ruth&nbsp;
just might get away with Javi's murder -- right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:39.520
up until Clare gives her up to Camila, that is.&nbsp;
This leads to Camila waiting at Ruth's home and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.520
in a shocking scene, killing&nbsp;
her with a pull of a trigger.&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:49.280
Ruth's death leaves Three as the sole survivor&nbsp;
of the Langmores, though his storyline is left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:54.720
up in the air. Also unknown is what will happen&nbsp;
to Ruth's portion of the casino. It wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.600
surprising if her stakes in the company go to&nbsp;
Three, or even Rachel Garrison, who came back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:04.880
the Ozarks to help run the casino. Even if Rachel&nbsp;
doesn't get it, it was a nice surprise for fans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.000
see her back for the series finale.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.640
In the final scene, Mel Sattem shows up at&nbsp;
Marty and Wendy's house and reveals that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.400
finally pieced together Ben's murder.
However, just when it seems like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.560
Byrdes are finally going to go down&nbsp;
for one of their countless crimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:25.760
Jonah pulls up with a shotgun. The scene&nbsp;
ends with a black screen and a gunshot.&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.960
Fan theories will likely run wild&nbsp;
with this ending. But it's pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.520
evident that Jonah pulls the trigger and&nbsp;
the Byrdes get off scot-free. So much for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.440
going legit.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.160
For most of the series, audiences don't know&nbsp;
if the Byrde family members will live or die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.880
let alone reunite -- especially Marty,&nbsp;
as he is consistently put in harm's way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.920
Yet, against all odds, the Byrdes&nbsp;
make a deal with Camila and the FBI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.600
buying their freedom from the&nbsp;
cartel and immunity from the FBI.&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.160
Wendy continuously says her family is close&nbsp;
to making all their ambitions a reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:13.360
Though it took several years and many close&nbsp;
calls, she is right in the end. When Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.440
4 ends, the family is free to do whatever&nbsp;
they want with the rest of their lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.160
no longer taking orders from people who could&nbsp;
have them killed with a snap of a finger.
 

